From: ios14-lithium
Subject: [build] use the POSIX function syntax in the header generator

The original /bin/sh script used the bash-only `function name()` form.
Linux /bin/sh is dash. This changes no generated definitions.

diff --git a/bsd/sys/make_posix_availability.sh b/bsd/sys/make_posix_availability.sh
--- a/bsd/sys/make_posix_availability.sh
+++ b/bsd/sys/make_posix_availability.sh
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 # @APPLE_OSREFERENCE_LICENSE_HEADER_END@
 #
 
-function usage() {
+usage() {
     echo "Usage: $0 <output>" 1>&2
     exit 1
 }
